Overlay patch 0027: audio-bridge null-chain guards (reference 0027 ported;
Sync Wave 2 crash-fix class, same family as 0030). The audio thread calls
these every synth update; the bridge null-checked the PLAYER but not the
CHAIN — Ship::Context::GetInstance() is mContext.lock() (null during
teardown/init windows) and GetAudio() is briefly null, so
GetInstance()->GetAudio()->GetAudioPlayer() faulted (reference device SEGV
on OTRAudio_Thread, twice). Ghostship reaches it directly: the iOS quit
path (0021) calls exit(0) after Window->Close() WITHOUT joining the audio
thread, which keeps spinning through Context teardown. Guard the chain in
all six bridge functions. Capturing the shared_ptr also holds a strong ref
for the call, closing the race within each function. Unconditional (a
null-check is always correct; upstreamable).

--- a/libultraship/src/libultraship/bridge/audiobridge.cpp
+++ b/libultraship/src/libultraship/bridge/audiobridge.cpp
@@ -5,7 +5,15 @@
 extern "C" {
 
 int32_t AudioPlayerBuffered() {
-    auto audio = Ship::Context::GetInstance()->GetAudio()->GetAudioPlayer();
+    // GS_IOS (overlay 0027): the audio thread races Context teardown/init —
+    // GetInstance() (weak_ptr.lock()) or GetAudio() is briefly null and the
+    // chained call faulted (device SEGV, 0030's family). The captured
+    // shared_ptr also pins the Context for this call.
+    auto gsIosCtx = Ship::Context::GetInstance();
+    if (gsIosCtx == nullptr || gsIosCtx->GetAudio() == nullptr) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+    auto audio = gsIosCtx->GetAudio()->GetAudioPlayer();
     if (audio == nullptr) {
         return 0;
     }
